35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the ground is tricky! Only two firms bid, and they warn of clay slippage. The depot says we can’t hoard the center, so the schedule is tight.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, clay slippage confirms my fears. The data shows people avoid soft margins, and drainage is failing. We must design for the ground, not against it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, that sounds scary. I found the staff is very small now, but there are kind volunteers who help on weekends.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, the clay issue is serious. My data shows the civic hall apron has failed repeatedly, while the basin holds. We must prioritize durable hard surfaces over fragile planting.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the eastern avenue trees died from lack of water. The habitat fund won’t cover that. We must plan for ongoing care, not just planting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, that apron failure worries me. If the center can’t be hoarded, how do we protect it from the clay? @Benjamin, does the drainage fix help the schedule?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the drainage fix is non-negotiable. If we ignore the heat and water flow, the plan fails before the first spade hits the ground.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, the volunteers are very helpful, but the staff is so small. I worry they will be too tired to look after everything properly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the ledger confirms the strain. Planted ground costs triple to maintain. We must limit soft areas to where care is guaranteed, not assumed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that triple cost is exactly what I feared. The fund covers planting, not the water to keep it alive. We must budget for that gap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the center stays open, the clay risk is huge. @Minako, does limiting soft areas actually make the finish date realistic for us?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, keeping the center open is a logistical nightmare, but the crossing data demands it. We must route people on firm ground, not force them into mud.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, I am glad the volunteers are there. But with so few staff, will they have time to rest? I worry about their tiredness.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, their dedication is valuable, but we cannot rely on goodwill to offset structural decay. The data shows hard surfaces last longer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, their kindness is precious, but goodwill cannot pay for water. We must ensure the budget covers the daily care, not just the initial planting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But with only two firms and clay risks, can we actually finish on time? I need a realistic date before we commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the date is secondary to the design. If we ignore the drainage and foot traffic, we’ll be fixing it for decades. Let’s prioritize function over speed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want to make sure the people who care for the park are not too tired. I hope the plan is kind to them.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, kindness is essential, but durability is the foundation. We must build structures that last, so the staff isn’t constantly repairing failures.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, durability is vital, but only if the city can afford the upkeep. I worry the ribbon-cutting hides the true long-term burden.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
